# GitHub Issues & Project Workflow

All planning and active work is tracked on **GitHub Issues** and the
[project board](https://github.com/users/sekurado/projects/2). Completed Stories 1–30 are archived in
[`docs/DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md`](../../docs/DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md).

## Issue Types

| Type | When to create | Project field **Type** |
|------|----------------|------------------------|
| Story | New feature epic spanning multiple tasks | `Story` |
| Task | Single implementable unit of work | `Task` |
| Bug | Defect or regression | `Task` (or add a Bug label if used) |

## Workflow

1. **Plan mode** — create a GitHub Issue with the full spec in the body (no separate markdown files).
2. **Project** — add the issue to [Project #2](https://github.com/users/sekurado/projects/2).
3. **Fields** — set **Type** (Story or Task), **Story** (link to parent story issue for tasks), and **Status** (Todo → In Progress → Done). **Status lives only on the project board** — do not duplicate it in issue bodies.
4. **Start story** — when implementation on a story begins (branch opened or first task started), move the **Story** issue **Status** → **In Progress** on the project board.
5. **Start task** — **first action before any implementation** (see [Starting a task (agents)](#starting-a-task-agents) below). Move that **Task** issue **Status** → **In Progress** on the project board; only one task should be in progress at a time.
6. **Commit** — when task implementation is complete, **stop for user review** before committing. After approval, commit with subject line `<task_number>: <short description>` (e.g. `31_2: Schema, migration, repositories and label search`), move project **Status** to **Done**, and add `Closes #N` (or `Fixes #N`) in the commit body on its own line with **no trailing punctuation** (use `Closes #7`, not `Closes #7.`). GitHub closes the linked issue when that commit is **pushed** — on any branch, not only after merge to `main`. **Do not commit without explicit user approval.**
7. **Task complete checklist** — after the approved commit (and push, if the user requests it): (1) project **Status** → **Done** via GraphQL/`gh`; (2) confirm the issue closed — if `Closes #N` did not auto-close, close the issue manually or fix the keyword and push again. Do not leave project **Status** at In Progress or Todo after the implementation commit.
8. **Pull request** — open a PR to merge the branch into `main`. Do not repeat `Closes #N` if the task issue is already closed; reference the issue for traceability instead.
9. **Story complete** — when all child task issues are closed, close the story issue and update `docs/DESIGN.md` if architecture changed.

### Issue state vs project Status

| Signal | When it changes |
|--------|-----------------|
| Project **Status** → Done | User-approved task implementation commit is made |
| Issue **closed** | Pushed commit or merged PR contains `Closes #N` / `Fixes #N` (any branch) |

Do not use `Closes #N` until the task is actually complete. Do not leave project **Status** at In Progress after the implementation commit.

### Starting a task (agents)

When the user says **start next task**, names a task issue, or you begin work on a task:

1. **Move the project card first** — set that task's **Status** → **In Progress** on [Project #2](https://github.com/users/sekurado/projects/2) via GraphQL or `gh` (below). Do this **before** reading code for implementation, editing files, or running task-specific tests.
2. **First task on a story** — also move the parent **Story** issue **Status** → **In Progress** if it is still **Todo**.
3. **Do not skip or defer** — never assume a prior session moved the card; if it is still **Todo**, update it now. Tell the user the card was moved (include issue number).
4. **One task in flight** — only one task should be **In Progress** at a time.

Repo issue state (open/closed) is separate from project **Status** — closing keywords in commits do not move the board.

### Updating project Status (agents)

GitHub MCP `issue_write` + `issue_fields` updates **repo** issue fields only — it cannot set project board **Status**, **Type**, or **Story** (those live on [Project #2](https://github.com/users/sekurado/projects/2)).

To move cards programmatically, use the **GitHub GraphQL API** (`https://api.github.com/graphql`) with `GITHUB_SEKURADO_PAT` (or `GITHUB_TOKEN`) and the `updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue` mutation on `user(login: "sekurado").projectV2(number: 2)`. If `gh` is installed and authenticated with the `project` scope, `gh project item-edit` is an alternative.

Do not tell the user the board cannot be updated without trying GraphQL (or `gh`) first. Never log, echo, commit, or paste `GITHUB_SEKURADO_PAT`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, or any `ghp_` / `github_pat_` value — read tokens only from the environment inside scripts.

