## Rules for Agents

- Do **not** create or update files under `tasks/` — that folder was removed.
- Put the full acceptance criteria and spec in the issue body. Do not add a Story Status or task Status column — use the project **Status** field.
- Link child tasks to their parent story issue in the **Story** project field and in the task body.
- **Starting a task:** move project **Status** → **In Progress** as the **first** step (GraphQL/`gh`), before any implementation — see [Starting a task (agents)](#starting-a-task-agents).
- When starting a story (first task on that story), move the **Story** issue **Status** → **In Progress** on the project board too.
- When committing completed task work, **wait for explicit user approval** after implementation is ready for review. Then use subject line `<task_number>: <short description>`, add `Closes #N` in the commit body (no trailing period), move the task's project **Status** to **Done** in the **same session** via GraphQL/`gh`, and confirm the issue closed after push. **Never commit without user review.** Never leave project **Status** at In Progress or Todo after the implementation commit.
- Never add `Co-authored-by` (or any other trailer) to commit messages unless the user explicitly asks for it.
- After completing a story, update [`docs/DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md`](../../docs/DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md) if the roadmap changed.
